    <string name="feed_check_tls_failed">The secure connection to the server failed. Only the person who manages the server can fix it.</string>
    <string name="feed_check_tls_expired">The website’s security certificate has expired. Only the person who manages the server can renew it.</string>
    <string name="feed_check_tls_not_yet_valid">The website’s security certificate is not valid yet. First check that your phone’s date and time are correct.</string>
    <string name="feed_check_tls_hostname">The security certificate belongs to another name than this address. Check the address; otherwise the server needs to be reconfigured.</string>
    <string name="feed_check_tls_untrusted">Android does not recognize who issued the security certificate. The server may use an internal, self-signed or incomplete certificate.</string>
    <string name="feed_check_tls_plain_http">The server answers on this port, but without encryption (plain HTTP). If it is a server on your home network, you can use http:// instead.</string>
    <string name="feed_check_tls_not_password">This is about the connection to the server, not your password. Droidrops will never turn off this protection.</string>
    <string name="feed_check_timeout">The server takes too long to answer. It may be busy or offline. Try again in a few minutes.</string>
    <string name="feed_check_connection_refused">The server exists but refuses the connection. The service may be stopped, or the port in the address may be wrong.</string>
    <string name="feed_check_network_error">The connection was interrupted. Check your network, then try again.</string>
    <string name="feed_check_auth_required">This feed is protected. Enter the login and password given by the website, then check again.</string>
    <string name="feed_check_credentials_rejected">The server did not accept this login or password. Check capital letters and extra spaces.</string>
    <string name="feed_check_unsupported_auth">This server asks for another sign-in method (%1$s) than a login and password. If it is a service like FreshRSS, Nextcloud News or Miniflux, add it as an account instead.</string>
    <string name="feed_check_forbidden">The server received the request but refuses access to this address, even with a login. It may block apps or some regions.</string>
    <string name="feed_check_not_found">The website exists, but nothing is at this address. The feed may have moved.</string>
    <string name="feed_check_method_not_allowed">The server answers, but this address cannot be read. It is often the address of a service or an API, not of a feed. For FreshRSS, Nextcloud News, Miniflux and similar services, add an account from the Account tab instead.</string>
